  {
   "id": 17,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1700,
    1200
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    320
   ],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## wan-infinitetalk.json\n\nA talking head: our character speaks an audio file\n\n**Does:** a still **portrait** + an audio file -> a clip of the character speaking that audio (`WanInfiniteTalkToVideo`, InfiniteTalk single-speaker). The output **carries the audio** (aac) - a viewer's file with sound. Host: our on-box `wan2.1_i2v_720p_14B_fp8_scaled` with the InfiniteTalk patch applied (`model_patches/wan2.1_infiniteTalk_single_fp16`, 5.13 GB) + `wav2vec2-chinese-base` audio encoder + the lightx2v distill lora + umt5/VAE.\n**Measured (E15, 2026-10-11):** 81 frames (3.24 s of speech at 25 fps) in **210 s**; identity holds through speech (lip-band motion 1.9x forehead, articulation real); the patch applies to our 720p fp8 base, so the route's new weights are only ~5.3 GB. Reference = **portrait** (the E13c identity-knob lesson).\n**Knobs:** the **audio** on `LoadAudio` (replace `audio_speaker1_woman.mp3` - speech from TTS or recording; the audio is what drives the mouth); the **reference** (portrait, face clear); **`seconds`** on `PrimitiveFloat` (3.24 ships) - how much audio to speak. A `ComfyMathExpression` turns it into **`length`** rounded to the model's required 4n+1 (`floor((a*25-1)/4+0.5)*4+1`), so there is no hand arithmetic; raising it raises VRAM. **`audio_scale`** (1.0) for lip-sync strength; **`motion_frame_count`** (9). Sampling: 6 steps / euler / normal, **no `ModelSamplingSD3`** (the template has none). **fps is pinned at 25** on `CreateVideo` - InfiniteTalk's audio conditioning is resampled for 25-fps video in the node code, so any other fps would desync the mouth; it is deliberately not a knob.\n**Traps:** lip-sync was **human-confirmed** on the probe clip (E15, 2026-10-11); for your own audio, play the output mp4 (the audio is embedded). The clip speaks the FIRST `length` frames' worth of audio (`audio_start=0, `audio_end=length`): audio past that is never read, and audio shorter than the window is padded with the first audio frame (idle mouth) - so **trim your audio to `seconds`**. Longer audio = chain segments: feed this flow's output IMAGE batch into a second `WanInfiniteTalkToVideo`'s **`previous_frames`** (the official extend pattern); each continuation advances `length - motion_frame_count` frames (72 = 2.88 s at defaults - drop the node's `trim_image` leading frames when stitching), not a full segment. `single_speaker` needs no masks (masks are the two-speaker mode's region control). The patch loads through `ModelPatchLoader` from `models/model_patches/`.\n**Siblings:** `wan-animate-motion.json` (S15) drives motion from a *video*; this flow drives it from *audio*.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S32** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E15** in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*"
   ],
